WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:04.820
Wooh!

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:07.380
Oh!

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.600
So a common problem when playing ArcherySoft

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.360
is that people don't always call their hits.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.320
So having a reliable way

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.020
*laughs*

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.100
Having a reliable way to know that you hit somebody

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.160
would be rather effective

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.500
and a very reliable way would be a camera

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.840
in the end of the arrow.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:27.880
We are going to try to mount a GoPro

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.380
to the end of the arrow.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.700
Maybe I can hit Wren right now.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.180
Ready?

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:34.920
yeah

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:36.860
*laughs*

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.980
*music*

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.100
*sounds of tape ripping and low conversation*

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.400
*stab stab stab*

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.060
Eugh!

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.000
*tape snapping, box hitting floor*

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:52.820
Oh, whoa!

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:54.360
What?

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.080
What's going on?

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:55.720
What are these?

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.460
What are these??

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:57.980
I don't know

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.000
Woaaaah!

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:00.020
*toy hits wall*

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.580
Oooooh!

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:02.460
What the heck?

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:03.780
I'm gonna try that one

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.640
That's so spooky

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.140
Woah!

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.200
*screams*

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:07.460
*screams again*

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.580
Somebody sent us an email

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.240
like a month ago

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.940
Xshot sent us an email like

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.220
Hey we make all these dart guns

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.100
and we're like that's cool

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:14.940
and they're like can we send you some?

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.760
and we're like, yea!

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.680
And that's that story.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.680
*all laughing*

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:19.560
They do work

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.680
and they do work with our current nerf dart selection

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.220
They're not quite as high tech

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:26.360
but it'll be good to have around for when we need like

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.900
a couple extra single shots.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.640
Give it a shot

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.920
Give it an Xshot

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:31.920
*plastic gun cocking*

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.500
Alright range test

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:38.740
Kind of like a hammershot

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.860
They hold a couple shots but they're single shot

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.440
Pretty accurate though

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:43.560
Yea not too bad

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.180
So let's get things started here.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:46.400
Here's my GoPro

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.400
*crafting montage music*

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:50.460
Cool

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.260
Let's see if this carves it out at all

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.260
*dremel whining over montage music*

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.740
Nick, how have you been enjoying your time

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.900
working on the Sam and Niko channel?

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.260
What have you learned about vlog film making?

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.580
Is there a pro tip you can give to people watching the vlog

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:18.640
if they want to edit their own?

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.700
You know that's the biggest point of feedback I have for anybody

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.980
when they ask me to look at their work

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:26.260
is like, it's too long

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.100
cut cut cut.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.620
Good rule of thumb when editing something and determining pacing is

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:33.460
say verbally what you're trying to convey on screen

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.560
"The character stands up and walks out of the room."

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.980
If the shot takes longer to do that

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:39.740
than it does for you to say what happens

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.640
the shot's too long.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.100
What are you going to put in there?

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:52.020
GoPro

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.540
I mean ... smart if you have more than one.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.040
It's just a matter of pulling this up on the outside

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.460
but I don't think we're going to get much out of that.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:02.960
*beep*

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:03.460
Oops

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.340
We have these little floaties

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.940
This will slip over here

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.420
In an efficient manner

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.280
There we have it.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.500
GoPro arrow mount

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.320
It works!

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.460
October is over

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.120
I'm still alive

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.460
I have a daughter

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:27.760
We shot everything that we needed to shoot

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.120
and the company didn't go under

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:32.740
*clicks tongue*

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.940
Tears of joy.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.440
Feeling a lot better about November

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.960
than I was about October

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.560
Something that you guys never know

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.320
is that footage gets lost every now and then

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.480
We don't know how it happens

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.420
but when you shoot as much as we do and put out a new video every other day

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.380
Sometimes a scene that you shot a few days ago

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.280
just kind of disappears and no one knows where it went

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.780
One of those things is this gun right here

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.240
*pained sound*

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.160
A fan actually painted this gun

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.520
with the Corridor logo and sent it ...

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.020
*board clatters*

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.220
And what's cool is he also like

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.880
modified it so it's actually a stronger gun than normal

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.800
We wanted to give a cool shoutout to the guy who made this and stent it to us

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:10.700
If you're the one who actually sent this to us

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.020
please leave a comment on this video

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.840
and we'll be sure to send you something pretty cool

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.920
It might just be a nerf dart that we signed

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.960
It might be ... our entire raid server

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:21.660
Probably won't be that one

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:25.180
I don't know how well this is going to fly yet

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:26.340
I think it'll be ok.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.780
It's going to be...

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:29.580
...great.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.120
First test here we go. Ready?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.880
Three, two, one

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:38.900
So the GoPro actually came out just a little bit

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.720
of its enclosure right there

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:41.940
Here we go!

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.100
Hey that was pretty good

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.540
I feel like the ultimate test

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:49.780
is to shoot it as high as it can possibly go

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:51.740
and to see it go up and arc and come back down.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.260
There's a lot of cars around here

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.060
Then don't hit the cars

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:56.080
Okay!

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.500
Wren's going to try to catch it, if he doesn't then we might break the GoPro

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.460
So big stakes here

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.540
No pressure

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:01.320
Say goodbye to this GoPro

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.440
GoPro, I hope you make it back from this journey

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.660
You're the first one of your kind to ever go into space

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.060
*kissing sound*

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:08.920
Kiss, Wren

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.180
*omph*

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.180
Three, two

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.640
*whooshing*

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:17.360
Wooh!

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:19.120
Nicely done!

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:20.120
That was great!

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.820
Here we go! Three two one

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:27.440
Oh that was perfect!

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:28.320
Alright, Wren

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:28.820
Run

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:30.040
Run to your brother!

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:32.480
*augh!*

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:33.640
*laughs*

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:37.380
You got my elbow!

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.020
We got a little scuff on the GoPro

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.020
Oh teh noes!

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:43.160
Everybody on the Sam and Niko channel really appreciates what you do for us

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.140
*groans*

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:50.380
*groans in slow motion*

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.200
That actually really hurt

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.660
I have a numb thumb

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.260
Since I got to shoot at you a whole bunch

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.440
you may now shoot at me

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.120
*laughs*

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.280
That was a slap!

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.860
That was satisfying actually

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.320
When I was a camp counselor for five years of my life

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.040
we had archery

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:09.840
and I was the archery instructor for one summer

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.480
So I say that now, but I'm going to be terrible.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:15.080
Do we have a... Do I... Is this right?

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.860
It's like a solid 40 feet

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:18.420
Really?

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:19.680
Maybe 50?

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:23.060
Here we go

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.420
That was like almost pretty close!

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.800
That was almost- That was not terrible

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.740
as my parents would say to me

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:33.460
growing up

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.000
Do you want to be shot at?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.060
Yeah I'll be shot at

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:39.120
I do want to shoot him.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.000
Remember that I love you.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.220
I love you very much

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:43.920
My last words

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.260
are pepperoni.

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:46.840
That's what I want on my tombstone.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:47.640
Ready?

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:48.940
Woah!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.780
That was right at you!

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:56.920
Good catch!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.640
Well that was my matrix dodge

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:00.500
The bumpers worked

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.240
It gracefully bounced down the street.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:04.080
Thank you guys very much, that was nice of you.

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:11.420
Bye! Bye, CorridorDigital! Goodbye!

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:13.100
About to see the footage for the first time.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.440
Sixty frames per second means you can actually do some slow motion

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:17.480
Woahh

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:19.580
That's really cool

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.180
Zooooooooooof

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.240
Look at that twist

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:27.200
So I'm manually twisting it at the opposite rate it spins

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.260
so you'll see the arrow spinning around the edge of the frame

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.900
but the world will stay flat

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.660
Oh that kind of creates a really cool effect

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:35.560
Yea it's really trippy

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:46.940
It was a success technically

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.540
But I would love to have like a more powerful arrow

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.880
on a more powerful bow

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.480
and shoot a GoPro even further.

